From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DeepSeek Harness <noreply@deepseek.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 00:58:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Move backup to a sidebar page and show whole-run progress

The desktop backup settings lived in a section of the settings page even
though a run deserves a page of its own, and the status line took its
percentage from the current file's bytes, so it fell back to 0% whenever
the uploads moved on. The sidebar now has a 备份 page that keeps every
backup row there: schedule, folders, encryption mode, passphrase,
recipients, signing key and the manual run.

Its progress card shows one bar and percentage for the whole run from
RunDone/RunTotal, the bytes done and total, the file in flight and a live
upload speed sampled from those same whole-run bytes. It never lists the
files one by one, so the progress no longer restarts with every file.

